        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "That's the whole structure, about fifteen lines. Add climbs by adding the low bit. Prefix descends by stripping it. Both loops run at most log n times, because each step changes the lowest set bit's position. A range sum is two prefix sums subtracted. To build from an array, call add n times, O of n log n.",
          "props": {
            "title": "The <em>code</em>",
            "file": "fenwick.cpp",
            "tag": "C++",
            "lang": "cpp",
            "size": 21,
            "width": 1150,
            "code": "struct Fenwick {\n    int n;\n    vector<long long> t;                  // 1-indexed: t[0] unused\n    Fenwick(int n) : n(n), t(n + 1) {}\n    void add(int i, long long d) {        // a[i] += d\n        for (; i <= n; i += i & -i)       // climb: add the low bit\n            t[i] += d;\n    }\n    long long prefix(int i) const {       // a[1] + ... + a[i]\n        long long s = 0;\n        for (; i > 0; i -= i & -i)        // descend: strip the low bit\n            s += t[i];\n        return s;\n    }\n    long long sum(int l, int r) const {   // a[l..r]\n        return prefix(r) - prefix(l - 1);\n    }\n};",
            "highlights": [
              {
                "at": "structure",
                "lines": "3",
                "note": "One array, 1-indexed"
              },
              {
                "at": "climbs",
                "lines": "5-7",
                "note": "add: climb by the low bit"
              },
              {
                "at": "descends",
                "lines": "9-13",
                "note": "prefix: strip the low bit"
              },
              {
                "at": "subtracted",
                "lines": "16",
